Trulli is the same as Toyota and Honda.

05:35:36.710 --> 05:35:40.170
That's right.

05:35:40.170 --> 05:35:42.170
In the preliminary round,

05:35:42.170 --> 05:35:48.170
Trulli showed the same performance as the top 3.

05:35:48.170 --> 05:35:52.170
The challenge is the pace of this machine.

05:35:52.170 --> 05:35:54.170
That's right.

05:35:54.170 --> 05:36:00.000
Trulli's tire protection is very good.

05:36:00.000 --> 05:36:07.960
How good is the setting of the car at such a difficult stage?

05:36:07.960 --> 05:36:15.900
How good is the balance of the car at the end of the race?

05:36:15.900 --> 05:36:22.200
How good is the setting of the pinpoints?

05:36:22.200 --> 05:36:30.000
I thought the tires were not fast enough in the first half.

05:36:30.000 --> 05:36:36.600
He's running at the expected pace from the beginning to the end in the middle of 18 seconds.

05:36:36.600 --> 05:36:53.840
I think that's okay in a way, but one of the challenges is to increase the pace during the race when you have to do it here, like Alonso, and when the car becomes wider, it becomes stronger, right?

05:36:53.840 --> 05:36:55.160
That's right.

05:37:00.800 --> 05:37:04.800
It's the 70th race of the F1 Grand Prix.

05:37:04.800 --> 05:37:06.800
There are 3 laps left.

05:37:06.800 --> 05:37:09.590
The top is Fernando Alonso.

05:37:09.590 --> 05:37:11.760
He's in 6th place.

05:37:11.760 --> 05:37:16.320
He keeps the gap with Raikkonen, who's in 2nd place.

05:37:16.320 --> 05:37:19.320
He's in 4th place until the bottom.

05:37:19.320 --> 05:37:21.320
There are 3 laps left.

05:37:21.320 --> 05:37:23.280
Moriaki-san, again,

05:37:23.280 --> 05:37:25.280
Renaud Alonso is perfect so far.

05:37:25.280 --> 05:37:27.290
He's perfect.

05:37:27.290 --> 05:37:30.000
Including the team,

05:37:30.000 --> 05:37:40.330
It was a close one, but the team's work was really perfect.

05:37:40.330 --> 05:37:47.220
Ukyo-san, the Canadian Grand Prix was a double-retire, and the American Grand Prix was a no-point.

05:37:47.220 --> 05:37:52.560
It's like you're coming back to Europe and you're going to catch the flow again.

05:37:52.560 --> 05:38:00.000
The flow changed suddenly after the first half, so I wanted to pull it together again.

05:38:00.000 --> 05:38:02.000
In order to win the championship again,

05:38:02.000 --> 05:38:08.820
he has to win the national team Grand Prix.

05:38:08.820 --> 05:38:11.820
In that sense, the driver is really focused today.

05:38:11.820 --> 05:38:17.050
He's doing a perfect job as Moriaki-san.

05:38:17.050 --> 05:38:20.900
Moriaki-san is 23 years old.

05:38:20.900 --> 05:38:23.900
Aronson is expected to be the youngest champion in the world.

05:38:23.900 --> 05:38:25.910
How do you feel as a driver?

05:38:25.910 --> 05:38:27.910
I think this is wonderful.

05:38:27.910 --> 05:38:30.000
As Ukyo-san said earlier,

05:38:30.060 --> 05:38:35.100
He expressed that he was afraid of the end of the race, but that kind of feeling is amazing.

05:38:35.100 --> 05:38:39.100
How good of a driver will he become in the future?

05:38:39.100 --> 05:38:40.100
Yes.

05:38:40.100 --> 05:38:45.830
Now, the team staff can see a smile.

05:38:45.830 --> 05:38:51.440
From the start of the position, he noticed the development of the top 6.

05:38:51.440 --> 05:38:53.430
23-year-old Fernandes Alonso.

05:38:54.450 --> 05:39:00.000
It is a Renault that looks richly flowing in the North American land.

05:39:00.570 --> 05:39:05.880
This big supporter is watching from France.

05:39:05.880 --> 05:39:08.710
He's now in the final lap at the top.

05:39:08.710 --> 05:39:11.800
The stands are also excited.

05:39:11.800 --> 05:39:14.330
80,000 spectators.

05:39:14.330 --> 05:39:19.470
Among them, 6,000 people are from FUNO.

05:39:19.470 --> 05:39:23.350
The big supporter is watching from the pole position.

05:39:23.350 --> 05:39:25.810
Today is an overwhelming speed.

05:39:25.810 --> 05:39:30.000
He showed the rigidity of the tires in the middle.

05:39:30.220 --> 05:39:33.180
He improved a lot in the machine part as well.

05:39:33.930 --> 05:39:39.620
Today, Fernando Alonso is the runner-up even in the 4th place, Baton.

05:39:39.620 --> 05:39:46.470
2nd place Raikkonen, 3rd place Michael Schumacher.

05:39:46.470 --> 05:39:49.320
However, we can't see that figure.

05:39:49.320 --> 05:39:52.340
Fernando Alonso, 23 years old.

05:39:52.340 --> 05:39:57.830
Final lap to become the youngest champion in the world.

05:39:57.830 --> 05:40:00.000
Oh, he took the step visor here.

05:40:00.860 --> 05:40:02.860
I want to see your happy voice clearly!

05:40:02.860 --> 05:40:04.860
That kind of feeling comes to me!

05:40:04.860 --> 05:40:08.190
Fernando Alonso, Final lap!

05:40:08.190 --> 05:40:15.660
Only a few moments left until the next moment!

05:40:15.660 --> 05:40:18.680
Renault had a bad flow in the U.S. league.

05:40:18.680 --> 05:40:20.680
Once again, here in Bokoku!

05:40:20.680 --> 05:40:24.290
The point leader is still strong!

05:40:24.290 --> 05:40:27.150
Alonso, European Grand Prix line!

05:40:27.150 --> 05:40:29.060
Top checker for the first time in three games!

05:40:31.340 --> 05:40:33.270
This is the 5th win of the season.

05:40:33.270 --> 05:40:36.920
Finally, we can see the title of the youngest.

05:40:36.920 --> 05:40:49.200
It's the first time in 22 years for Clavio Briatore to win a national championship.

05:40:49.200 --> 05:40:52.820
And Kimi Raikkonen.

05:40:52.820 --> 05:40:58.480
From the 13th grid where he won hard, he made a 2nd checker.

05:40:58.480 --> 05:41:00.000
Oh, Carlos Ghosn.

05:41:02.970 --> 05:41:11.640
Michael Schumacher got a checker in 3rd place.

05:41:11.640 --> 05:41:12.770
Here is the result.

05:41:12.770 --> 05:41:14.950
Hernando Alonso got 10,005 points.

05:41:14.950 --> 05:41:15.810
Raikkonen got 2nd place.

05:41:15.810 --> 05:41:18.820
Michael Schumacher got 3,000 points in a row.

05:41:18.820 --> 05:41:20.000
Baton got 4th place.

05:41:20.000 --> 05:41:23.040
B.A.R. Honda got the first point of the season.

05:41:23.040 --> 05:41:24.180
Toyota got 5th place.

05:41:24.180 --> 05:41:26.550
Ralph got 7th place.

05:41:26.550 --> 05:41:28.050
Takuma Sato got 11th place.

05:41:28.050 --> 05:41:30.000
15 French Grand Prix cars were completed.

05:41:31.370 --> 05:41:40.490
He's strong because he's the leader of the point team, the mother country of Renault.

05:41:40.490 --> 05:41:44.520
Fernando Alonso, his 5th win of the season.

05:41:44.520 --> 05:41:49.910
He's a great supporter.

05:41:49.910 --> 05:41:59.020
Mr. Moriaki, when you won the European Grand Prix, there was a sense of luck that you were going to retire next year, but this time you were able to win with your strength.

05:41:59.020 --> 05:42:00.000
That's right.

05:42:00.600 --> 05:42:05.560
I feel that the strength of the start of the season has returned completely.

05:42:05.560 --> 05:42:08.880
And Kimi Daikonen is second place from the 13th grid.

05:42:08.880 --> 05:42:11.050
That's right.

05:42:11.050 --> 05:42:12.740
He cheered me up today.

05:42:12.740 --> 05:42:14.520
That's right.

05:42:16.330 --> 05:42:25.250
Michael Schumacher is now in third place, but the point leader is a top checker after three games.

05:42:30.000 --> 05:42:33.430
TAKUMA and ALONSO have 10.5 wins.

05:42:33.430 --> 05:42:37.360
They won the first round of the summer European championship.

05:42:37.360 --> 05:42:38.290
Mr.Nagai.

05:42:38.290 --> 05:42:39.630
Yes.

05:42:39.630 --> 05:42:47.630
Well, in the end, ALONSO, RIKONEN, MIHAIRO, SHIWAMAHA, and DRIVERS RANKING were ranked in order.

05:42:47.630 --> 05:42:50.640
However, TAKUMA was unfortunately a grand prize.

05:42:50.640 --> 05:42:52.640
It was a very unfortunate result.

05:42:52.640 --> 05:42:56.640
I was able to see TAKUMA's aggressive run as a samurai.

05:42:56.640 --> 05:42:58.640
I feel like I'm back in shape.

05:42:58.640 --> 05:43:00.000
So I look forward to the second half.

05:43:00.000 --> 05:43:07.010
That's right, and for BR Honda, it's the first point of this season, so I'm looking forward to the second half of the race.

05:43:07.010 --> 05:43:10.230
And Yu-chan, Raikkonen came in second place.

05:43:10.230 --> 05:43:19.770
Yes, it was really the start of the 13th, but I don't think there was an engine replacement because it was the 2nd place of Raikkonen, but it was really amazing.

05:43:19.770 --> 05:43:23.040
I did it, right? I'm looking forward to the next British Grand Prix.

05:43:23.040 --> 05:43:26.960
I would like to look forward to the second round. And Ukyo-san, how was it?

05:43:26.960 --> 05:43:30.000
Well, Alonso, with this young age, this running.

05:43:30.000 --> 05:43:32.820
It's like watching Michail when he was young.

05:43:32.820 --> 05:43:38.890
And Mr. Moriaki, I think it was the Alonso Grand Prix.

05:43:38.890 --> 05:43:45.560
But Kimi Raikkonen came out from 13th place and went up to the podium.

05:43:45.560 --> 05:43:51.050
I don't know what will happen in the second half. It was a very good Grand Prix.

05:43:51.050 --> 05:43:57.060
There is also the appearance of Alain Prost at the podium, but it is the first time in 22 years that Renault works has won the country Grand Prix.

05:43:57.060 --> 05:44:00.000
Manicure is wrapped in blue air.

05:44:02.140 --> 05:44:04.640
Next is the UK Grand Prix.

05:44:04.640 --> 05:44:08.140
Takuma's second home is where he lives.

05:44:08.140 --> 05:44:11.140
For his teammate, Baton, it's a country Grand Prix.

05:44:11.140 --> 05:44:14.140
Mr. Fukio, please tell us what you think of the UK Grand Prix.

05:44:14.140 --> 05:44:18.650
It is the ultimate high-speed circuit in the Grand Prix circuit.

05:44:18.650 --> 05:44:23.650
For Takuma, who became the champion of the UK F3, it is a course that he is really used to.

05:44:23.650 --> 05:44:27.650
And for his teammate, Baton, I really look forward to winning the championship twice in a row.

05:44:27.650 --> 05:44:30.000
This is Takuma's second hometown, where he has many fans.

05:44:30.000 --> 05:44:32.760
I hope you will do your best in F1.

05:44:32.760 --> 05:44:39.340
The final of the 11th F1 British Grand Prix will be broadcast on Sunday, July 10th at 11:50pm.

05:44:39.340 --> 05:44:43.960
And in August, the first F1 event will be held at the Turco Grand Prix.

05:44:43.960 --> 05:44:48.310
F1 will cross the Ege Sea this summer!

05:44:48.310 --> 05:44:53.360
F1 will be the first to land in Istanbul, the land of oil and gas civilization!

05:44:53.360 --> 05:44:55.830
The first F1 Turco Grand Prix on the market!

05:44:55.830 --> 05:44:58.040
You will be a witness to history!

